_verify_artifact_impl and never run; the pre-merge check was a standalone call,
not the conductor's path. A task completed at 20:50Z and exp7031's artifact reads
flagged_adversarial None with a clean live re-check.

Stated with its limits: that shows the gate does not break the normal path or
manufacture a quarantine. It does not exercise the new CRITICALs, which fire only
on an artifact declaring a class, and none does yet -- 0 of 6024, measured. Those
stay unexercised by construction under a forward-only cutover.

Separately, BLOCK moved 11 to 12, its first movement today, an hour after that
merge. It is not the gate: the erasure guard caught a task reverting a file and
restored it. That BLOCK counts a save. The first inference available was "I merged
a gate an hour ago and now BLOCK moved", which is the correlation this check's own
instructions require refusing until the base rate is measured.

Fourth dashboard-semantics defect, joining the batch: the `today` line counts
"something went wrong" and "a guard did its job" the same way. Not written to
memory -- the general principle is recorded there three times already and a fourth
clause is accretion; the decision is noted so it reads as considered, not
forgotten.

